  <worksheets>
    <worksheet name='Sheet 1'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true'>Foundry-level process Inflection Timeline with EUV Adoption</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This figure illustrates major semiconductor process-node introductions by leading foundries over time. The horizontal axis represents the year of first high-volume manufacturing, while the vertical axis groups data by foundry. Marker shape denotes the dominant transistor architecture at each process generation (Planar, FinFET, and Gate-All-Around), and marker size indicates whether extreme ultraviolet (EUV) lithography was employed at introduction. Larger markers correspond to EUV-enabled processes, highlighting the timing and role of EUV adoption as a key technological inflection point in advanced-node scaling.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
